      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">50 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span><span class=\"chip\">Arrays</span><span class=\"chip\">Hash map</span><span class=\"chip\">O(n)</span></div>\r\n  <h1>Prefix sums: subarray sum K, difference arrays, prefix XOR</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">One running total answers \"sum of any range\" in O(1). Add a hash map of the totals you have already seen and it counts subarrays with sum k, finds the longest balanced block, handles \"multiple of k\" with remainders, and walks down a tree for Path Sum III. Run it backwards and you get the difference array (car pooling, range add). Swap + for XOR and it all still works. Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\r\n"
  },
